/u/208281322?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/kaoru0822-kitauji", "html_url": "https://github.com/kaoru0822-kitauji", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kaoru0822-kitauji/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kaoru0822-kitauji/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kaoru0822-kitauji/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kaoru0822-kitauji/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kaoru0822-kitauji/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kaoru0822-kitauji/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kaoru0822-kitauji/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kaoru0822-kitauji/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kaoru0822-kitauji/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "open", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 1, "created_at": "2026-10-15T04:16:17Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-15T05:00:36Z", "closed_at": null, "assignee": null, "author_association": "COLLABORATOR", "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "**Summary:** semantic analysis of one shipped bundle fails with `RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded` on current `main`. The exception is not deep recursion: it comes from `possibleResults.push(...getterResultReferences(…))` in `semanticClassPropertyReferences` (`javascriptSemanticObjectReferences.ts`), when the spread array exceeds V8's argument limit. Removing the spread does not fix it. The same file then runs for **340 s and exhausts an 8 GB heap**, because getter-result expansion grows combinatorially.\n\n**Artifact (shipped, not attached):** Claude for macOS 2.37337.1, `app.asar` → `.vite/build/index.chunk-e5zmsebk.js`, 1,296,396 B, SHA-256 `a49783e6f17fafcde3ee7fe072a7864b11cadbea918bd2d9a15f95b9311cae7f`. It contains a bundled undici-style `Request` class whose getters return fields of a symbol-keyed state object:\n\n```js\nget method(){return P.brandCheck(this,U),this[M].method}\nget redirect(){return P.brandCheck(this,U),this[M].redirect}\nget body(){return P.brandCheck(this,U),this[M].body?this[M].body.stream:null}\n// … many more\n```\n\n**Observed** (`analyzeParsedJavaScriptSemantics`, Node 26.5, macOS arm64):\n- `main` (4135c91): throws `RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded` after ~2.3 s. The trace runs `collectSemanticMemberMutationsSteps` → `markEscaped` → `escapedReferenceLeaves` → `expandedValues` → `referencedValues` → `semanticClassPropertyReferences` ⇄ `getterResultReferences`, only about 6 frames deep.\n- I instrumented `getterResultReferences`: individual calls return **2,282** references over only **7** distinct nodes, with paths that are permutations of getter names, e.g. `[\"reloadNavigation\",\"body\",\"stream\",\"redirect\",\"referrerPolicy\",\"destination\",\"method\"]` and `[\"mode\",\"body\",\"stream\",\"credentials\",\"referrerPolicy\",\"destination\",\"method\"]`, each repeated many times.\n- With the spread replaced by a loop, the file did not finish: 340 s, then a V8 heap OOM at ~8 GB.\n\n**Likely mechanism:** `this[M]` reads with a computed key that is unknown statically, so it can match any accessor of the class. Each matched getter's result again reads `this[M].<field>`, and the expansion enumerates orderings of getter names. The per-getter guard in `getterResultReferences` (`previousLength <= path.length`) stops revisiting one getter with a non-shrinking path, but it doesn't bound the number of distinct orderings across many getters.\n\n**Scope notes:**\n- The other 420 Claude.app files, plus Discord, Notion, Signal, Tabby (2,183 files, including unbundled undici 8.10.2) and VS Code `out/`, analyze normally.\n- A rolldown bundle of undici 8.10.2's `index-fetch.js` (412 KB) also analyzes fine (540 ms), so the trigger needs more of this chunk's surrounding code. I don't have a public minimal reproduction yet.\n- In the CLI the semantic phase runs in the JavaScript worker, so this file loses its semantic facts rather than crashing the process.\n\n**Expected:** getter-result expansion should be bounded (for example by a per-query reference budget, or by collapsing unknown-key receiver reads to one conservative effect), with exhaustion reported as unknown coverage rather than an exception or unbounded growth. Two separate safety fixes also seem worthwhile: `push(...array)` on unbounded reference lists in this module should become a loop, and an unknown computed key on `this` should probably not fan out to every accessor.\n", "closed_by": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/morluto/rea/issues/3839/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/morluto/rea/issues/3839/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "pinned_comment": null}, "comments": [{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/morluto/rea/issues/comments/6184793162", "html_url": "https://github.com/morluto/rea/issues/3839#issuecomment-6184793162", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/morluto/rea/issues/3839", "id": 6184793162, "node_id": "IC_kwDOSB6hVc8AAAABcKR0Sg", "user": {"login": "XinwangTao", "id": 162271420, "node_id": "U_kgDOCawQvA", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/162271420?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/XinwangTao", "html_url": "https://github.com/XinwangTao", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XinwangTao/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XinwangTao/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XinwangTao/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XinwangTao/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XinwangTao/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XinwangTao/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XinwangTao/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XinwangTao/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XinwangTao/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-10-15T05:00:36Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-15T05:00:36Z", "body": "Thanks for the detailed write-up — the mechanism makes sense: an unknown computed key like this[M] matching every accessor turns getter-chain exploration into a permutation problem, and the previousLength <= path.length guard only stops revisiting one getter, not the combinatorial blowup across distinct orderings. I agree bounding the expansion is the right direction; a per-query reference budget plus memoizing already-expanded (receiver, path) pairs would keep the worst case predictable without losing current dedup behaviour. Would be curious whether #3846/#3848 take the budget approach or the conservative-collapse for unknown-key reads.", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/morluto/rea/issues/comments/6184793162/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}]}